solnix patch (not upstream, 2026-11-12): parse process.config on first access instead of during bootstrap.

config.gypi holds the install prefix (variables.node_prefix = configure --prefix). bootstrap/node.js parsed it into
process.config while node_mksnapshot built the startup snapshot, so the snapshot held $out as a heap string, under V8's
snapshot checksum (blob bytes 8..11). When the prefix is rewritten after the build (Nix --check's scratch out, CA
outputs; nixpkgs sets __contentAddressed = false for "Check failed: VerifyChecksum(blob)"), the string is fixed and the
checksum is not. Measured: it was the blob's only $out occurrence (v24.18.0, offset 0x129087).

process.config keeps its value, its frozen objects and its final attributes: the getter replaces itself with the same
data property (enumerable, configurable, read-only) on first access. process.features.typescript reads node_use_amaro
when it is first asked for. Upstream main (2026-11-12) still parses it during bootstrap.

--- a/lib/internal/bootstrap/node.js	2026-11-12 11:32:59.466608208 -0500
+++ b/lib/internal/bootstrap/node.js	2026-11-12 11:32:59.478729216 -0500
@@ -129,21 +129,37 @@
